  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that rna_only with scvi_n200, multiprofile, and transformer aggregation achieves the best accuracy (0.653, config_006), while image-only (resnet50) is very weak (0.208). The critical unresolved question is whether the image modality, even if weak in isolation, provides complementary information that improves on the RNA-only baseline. Config_032 takes the exact best RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) and adds resnet50 image features with concat fusion, changing only the model setting from rna_only to multimodal. This isolates the effect of adding the image modality. With 3 experiments remaining, this is the highest-value test: if it improves over 0.653, the remaining budget can explore multimodal variants (e.g., weighted fusion, ViT image encoder); if it does not, it confirms RNA-only is optimal and we can stop exploring image-based configurations."
}

